<title>SPAIN: Spanish Treasury announces May bond tenders.</title>
<headline>Spanish Treasury announces May bond tenders.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain announced on Monday  BANDF the amount of notes and bonds the Spanish Treasury would tender at its monthly auctions on Tuesday and Wednesday. Following are the minimum and maximum amounts:</p>
<p>(in billions of pesetas)</p>
<p>ISSUE	   Expected amount   Maximum amount     Auction date</p>
<p>3 and 10-yr	300		    375		  May 6</p>
<p>5 and 15-yr	185		    225		 May 7</p>
<p>April auctions	amount announced   allotted</p>
<p>01/4 (3- and 10-year)	275 - 340	335 *</p>
<p>02/4 (5- and 15-year)	150 - 190	150 *</p>
<p>* This is the amount actually sold on the market and includes the second segment of the auction.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
